ZCL_COMMAND_READY_COMMAND(
    "fleet.steer.grant", "fleet.steer", "",
    "Mint and revoke the adapter's scoped bearer grants",
    "mint draws 128 CSPRNG bits for one bearer id scoped to a subset of "
    "brief,send,evidence,terminate,deliver with a bounded lifetime (ttl_seconds 0..2592000, "
    "0 means no expiry) and appends it to the owner-private grant store; "
    "the id is returned exactly once and never echoed elsewhere. list "
    "inventories the store so the owner can see what there is to revoke: "
    "one row per grant with its label, scopes, created, expires, revoked "
    "and state, newest first in pages (limit 1..128, default 32; pass the "
    "returned next as before for the following page; truncated says more "
    "remain), and the id cut to an 8-character prefix "
    "so the listing is never itself a credential file (revoke still needs "
    "the whole 32). revoke "
    "appends a superseding revoked row (revoking twice re-affirms). "
    "Revoke drops queued work sent under the grant. A running row "
    "continues unless the grant's scopes include terminate, which ends "
    "that row's claim on later stages. "
    "unknown ids are refused, never silently accepted. A revoked or "
    "expired grant "
    "fails every fleet.steer verb with STEER_GRANT_REVOKED or "
    "STEER_GRANT_EXPIRED. peer=<roster name> (with a label and the send "
    "scope) mints an admission record instead of a bearer: it lets the "
    "receiver admit a directive that came over the signed fleet board from "
    "that enrolled box under that label, and is refused as a bearer "
    "(STEER_GRANT_PEER_ONLY). This governs only fleet.steer verbs: it is not "
    "wallet authority and not a fleet key role. It contacts no peer.", 32768,
    "fleet,steer,grant,list,revoke,bearer,scope,expiry,chatgpt",
    "zcl.fleet_steer_grant.input.v1", "zcl.fleet_steer_grant.v1",
    "action,scopes,ttl_seconds,label,id,peer,limit,before", "action",
    "z23 fleet steer grant --action=mint --scopes=brief,send",
    ZCL_COMMAND_LAYER_OPS, ZCL_COMMAND_EFFECT_MUTATE,
    ZCL_COMMAND_RISK_DEV_MUTATION, ZCL_COMMAND_SCOPE_LOCAL,
    ZCL_COMMAND_AUTH_OWNER, ZCL_COMMAND_MODE_SYNC,
    ZCL_COMMAND_LATENCY_FAST, ZCL_COMMAND_COST_LOW,
    ZCL_COMMAND_CONFIRM_NONE, ZCL_COMMAND_LANE_LOCAL,
    ZCL_COMMAND_CAP_DEV_STATE_WRITE, ZCL_COMMAND_TRAIT_NONE,
